# The := slice (the author's correction of 2026-11-07; the book, assign-known): `:=` writes a place already known -- an
# executable `zz := 5` where no place zz is known is the refusal at translation, not the definition of a field; the same
# form with a known place (int: x 1; x := 5) is the write (dyn/assign_known.lm2).
fn: f () int
    zz := 5
    return: 1
end: f
int: code 7
if: f() != 1
    code: 81
---
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
